---
/**
 * /service-areas/ — the areas hub.
 *
 * A separate top-level page from /services/, and linked from the homepage
 * alongside it. This is the directory of WHERE: every area the studio
 * serves, and every service available to clients travelling from it. The
 * services pages answer what; these answer from where.
 *
 * It replaced the nine standalone /service-areas/{area}/ pages, which were
 * each a general area page with no service attached. Under the new
 * architecture the service is the entry point — /service-areas/la-jolla/facial/ —
 * and this page is the mesh that makes every one of them reachable.
 *
 * It is also where the ten zero-demand area pages land after their 301,
 * so it lists every served area rather than only the ones with a page.
 */
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Reveal from '../../components/Reveal.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import NapBlock from '../../components/NapBlock.astro';
import BreadcrumbSchema from '../../components/schema/BreadcrumbSchema.astro';
import FaqSchema from '../../components/schema/FaqSchema.astro';
import FaqList from '../../components/FaqList.astro';
import RequestBand from '../../components/sections/RequestBand.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import SpeakableSchema from '../../components/schema/SpeakableSchema.astro';
import { areaShells } from '../../data/area-shells';
import { services } from '../../data/services';
import { getServiceAreasForArea } from '../../data/service-areas-index';
import { areaServicePath, areaPath } from '../../config/urls';
import { business, verifiedPrices } from '../../config/business';
import { CTA_LABEL } from '../../config/nav';
import heroServiceAreasHub from '../../assets/hero-service-areas-hub-san-diego-coverage-map-kiamo.jpg';
import VerifiedProof from '../../components/VerifiedProof.astro';
import { getServiceTestimonials } from '../../data/testimonials';

/**
 * The areas, grouped by the climate that shapes their skin concern.
 *
 * The grouping is the useful part: a client reading "coastal" learns
 * something a client reading a flat list of nine names does not — that the
 * barrier damage in Encinitas and the pigmentation in Chula Vista come from
 * the same distance from the marine layer, in opposite directions.
 */
/**
 * The questions.
 *
 * Value first, then the studio — the house rule the whole cluster follows.
 * The old set led with drive times and framed every answer around how far a
 * client had to come, which made the page an argument about the drive rather
 * than about the treatment. The distance is still in there, because it is a
 * real question, but it is never the frame.
 */
const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'How far do clients travel to reach KIAMO Skin?',
    answer:
      'Most clients drive between five and forty-five minutes. North Park and Hillcrest are under ten minutes with no freeway, and Pacific Beach, La Mesa and La Jolla are fifteen to twenty. Chula Vista and Del Mar run twenty to twenty-five minutes, and Encinitas and Carlsbad are the farthest at roughly thirty to forty on I-5. The KIAMO Skin studio is at 3067 Reynard Way in Mission Hills with free parking on site.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is there parking at the studio?',
    answer:
      'Free parking is available on site at the KIAMO Skin studio, so there is no street parking to find and no garage to pay for. The studio is by appointment only, which means a space is always available when a client arrives.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can I combine treatments to make one trip worth it?',
    answer:
      'Yes — combining is discussed at the first consultation when it makes clinical sense. A HydraFacial and dermaplaning can share a single appointment at KIAMO Skin. Procell microchanneling and a LIRA peel cannot be layered in one visit, because both work on the same surface and their recovery periods would overlap. The plan accounts for how often a round trip is realistic.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do I need to live nearby to get consistent results?',
    answer:
      'No. Clients from Carlsbad, Encinitas and Del Mar complete full corrective courses regularly. What decides it is scheduling the series as a block at the first appointment rather than booking visit by visit — a three-session microchanneling series at four-to-six-week intervals fits into a calendar whether the studio is ten minutes away or forty. KIAMO Skin sets the whole course at the first consultation for exactly that reason.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is the first appointment like?',
    answer:
      'A full consultation, a skin analysis and a first treatment, for $249 at KIAMO Skin. It takes longer than a follow-up, so it is worth leaving margin around it. After that appointment there is a written plan with the treatments in it, the intervals and the session count, and a realistic sense of how often a return is needed.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Which areas send the most clients to KIAMO Skin?',
    answer:
      'North Park, Pacific Beach and La Jolla send the most, followed by Chula Vista and La Mesa. North Park is the closest at three and a half miles with no freeway. Chula Vista sends the most pigmentation and melasma clients, which reflects the inland UV load and the skin demographics in that part of the county — and KIAMO Skin treats melasma there with gentle peels whose strength is raised only as the barrier allows.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Which treatment is right for my area?',
    answer:
      'Each area below lists the treatments with a page for it, and each page opens with what that treatment addresses for that area — the barrier damage salt air causes, the inland UV load, the congestion a coastal climate produces. The consultation still decides the modality, but the pages say which ones are worth the trip before anyone books.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Does KIAMO Skin offer mobile facial services in San Diego?',
    answer:
      'No, and KIAMO Skin will not. Mobile services cannot deliver clinical-grade corrective treatment: a HydraFacial Syndeo needs a dedicated water line and electrical setup, Procell microchanneling needs a sterile environment for post-treatment protocol, DMK enzyme therapy needs temperature control and a stable surface, and medical-grade LED therapy needs professional panels rather than handheld consumer devices. Convenience costs equipment quality, sterile conditions and corrective capability, and the studio is a single treatment room with one practitioner for a reason.',
  },
];

/**
 * The matrix.
 *
 * Each area, and under it every service with a page for it. This is the crawl
 * path into the cluster — every one of the twenty-five service-and-city
 * pages is one link from here, and every one is also reachable from its
 * service hub and its sibling pages.
 */
const matrix = areaShells.map((shell) => ({
  shell,
  rows: getServiceAreasForArea(shell.slug).map((record) => ({
    record,
    service: services.find((s) => s.slug === record.service),
  })),
}));

/** The areas that have at least one service page. */
const covered = matrix.filter((m) => m.rows.length > 0);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Areas We Serve in San Diego, CA | KIAMO Skin"
  description="KIAMO Skin is a licensed facial spa in Mission Hills, San Diego, serving 10 areas across the county. HydraFacial, peels, scalp therapy. From $199."
  headerTheme="dark"
>
  <BreadcrumbSchema slot="head" trail={[{ name: 'Areas We Serve', path: '/service-areas/' }]} />
  <FaqSchema slot="head" faqs={faqs} />
  <SpeakableSchema slot="head" />

  <article>
    {/* The hero. The coverage map is the background, the offer is the
        subject, and the action is in the first screen.

        It used to lead with the drive — "where clients travel from and what
        the drive is worth", "the honest distance from each". That framing
        makes the page an argument about travel rather than about treatment,
        and it is the wrong frame for a client already in the city. The
        studio's own city is now the first entry in the list below, and the
        hero says what the studio does. */}
    <PageHero
      eyebrow="San Diego, CA · One studio, off Washington Street"
      h1="Facial spa in San Diego, CA"
      claim="One studio in Mission Hills, and eleven areas it serves — including the city itself."
      paragraph="KIAMO Skin is a licensed facial spa at 3067 Reynard Way in Mission Hills. Every treatment is performed by Kiki, a California licensed esthetician with 7+ years in corrective skin work, in one private treatment room. Parking is free on site and the studio is appointment-only."
      image={heroServiceAreasHub}
      imageAlt="A coverage map of San Diego County showing the areas KIAMO Skin serves from its Mission Hills studio"
      price={{ label: 'First-time client treatment', price: verifiedPrices['first-time-client'] }}
      trust={[
        { label: 'Free parking on site' },
        { label: 'Eleven areas across the county' },
        { label: 'Prices published before a booking is made' },
        { label: 'Safe for every Fitzpatrick type, I–VI' },
      ]}
      reassurance={[
        business.visit.appointmentOnly,
        business.visit.parking,
        'Free cancellation up to 48 hours before',
      ]}
      ancestors={[{ name: 'Service Areas', path: '/service-areas/' }]}
      current="San Diego County"
      eventLabel="areas_hero"
    />

    <section class="bg-porcelain">
      <div class="wrap section-y">
        <p class="t-eyebrow text-ink-soft">Every treatment and area</p>
        <h2 class="t-h2 mt-5 max-w-[26ch]">
          All {covered.reduce((n, m) => n + m.rows.length, 0)} service-and-area pages
        </h2>
        <p class="t-body mt-6 max-w-[62ch]">
          Each page covers what that treatment addresses for that area, the honest drive time, and the
          local skin concern. Click through to find the client’s.
        </p>
        <ul class="m-0 mt-12 grid list-none gap-x-10 gap-y-0 p-0 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
          {
            covered.map(({ shell, rows }) => (
              <li class="border-b border-line">
                <p class="t-service pt-7 text-[1.0625rem]">
                  <a href={areaPath(shell.slug)} class="hover:text-rose">{shell.name}</a>
                </p>
                <ul class="m-0 list-none p-0">
                  {rows.map(({ record, service }) => (
                    <li>
                      <a
                        href={areaServicePath(record.area, record.service)}
                        class="t-body group flex items-baseline justify-between gap-x-4 py-3 transition-colors duration-300 hover:text-rose"
                      >
                        <span>{service?.name ?? record.service}</span>
                        <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-rose">
                          →
                        </span>
                      </a>
                    </li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    {/* The FAQ. */}

  {/* The proof.

      The rating and the review count appeared on exactly two pages of the
      site — the homepage and /reviews. Every commercial page argued for the
      studio in the studio's own voice. This band puts the objective figure
      and two client voices on the page, which is both what a reader deciding
      whether the drive is worth it needs, and what an answer engine weights. */}
  <section class="bg-blush py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-[68ch]">
        <Reveal>
          <p class="t-eyebrow text-ink-soft">From the treatment room</p>
          <h2 class="t-h2 mt-4 max-w-[26ch]">What clients say once they have been in.</h2>
        </Reveal>
        <div class="mt-10">
          <VerifiedProof quotes={getServiceTestimonials('areas')} />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

    <section class="bg-ivory">
      <div class="wrap section-y">
        <div class="max-w-[68ch]">
          <Reveal>
            <p class="t-eyebrow text-ink-soft">Common questions</p>
            <h2 class="t-h2 mt-5">Facials across San Diego County</h2>
          </Reveal>
          <div class="mt-12">
            {/* The first two answer in full on the page — how far clients
                travel, and whether parking is an issue — because they are
                what a reader from another city is deciding about. */}
            <FaqList faqs={faqs} openFirst={2} />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-porcelain py-16 md:py-20">
      <div class="wrap">
        <NapBlock />
      </div>
    </section>

    {/* The request. The directory answers "where"; this answers "how do I
        book", with the price and the button next to it. */}
    <RequestBand
      heading="Start in San Diego — with a price before a booking is made."
      eventLabel="areas_hub_band"
    />

    <script>
      import '../../scripts/scroll-depth';
    </script>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
